From 602fdd6693622c5450c73fcfb86877abd5658c33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(core): retain decode-frontier SWA checkpoints and order
 hybrid KV eviction tail-to-root

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 2756478b60b90700b9918b457aeb38657da637b5.

Rationale:
Multi-turn 64K-100K agent conversations with hybrid FullAttention (block_size=256) + SlidingWindow (block_size=128, window=128) KV cache and sparse prefix_cache_retention_interval (512 on tp3-triangle, 8192 on tp4-ring) lose prefix-cache hits across decode boundaries and under shared BlockPool eviction pressure due to three gaps in vllm/v1/core/:
1. Decode-frontier SWA checkpoint loss: SparseRetentionPolicy._retain only retained segment multiples (k * interval) and prompt boundaries (request.num_prompt_tokens). During decode (num_tokens > request.num_prompt_tokens), whenever a turn stopped at T_end with T_end % 256 >= 128 on a non-segment boundary, SlidingWindowManager.remove_skipped_blocks freed the 128-token SWA block at floor(T_end / 256) * 256 un-hashed before free() ran, causing the next turn to miss the decoded 256-token boundary.
2. Inverted root-before-tail LRU eviction order in the shared BlockPool: SlidingWindowManager.remove_skipped_blocks freed retained SWA checkpoints in ascending token order as the sliding window advanced, placing early SWA checkpoints (512, 8192) at the LRU head of free_block_queue (evicted first). In addition, SlidingWindowManager.add_local_computed_blocks only touched the 128-token window tail on a cache hit without refreshing earlier retained SWA checkpoints of the matched prefix, and HybridKVCacheCoordinator.free freed all Group 0 (FullAttentionManager) blocks before Group 1 (SlidingWindowManager) blocks instead of interleaving by descending token position. Evicting an early SWA checkpoint collapsed HybridKVCacheCoordinator.find_longest_cache_hit to that early segment even when all 256-token MLA blocks remained cached.
3. Un-cached boundary crossing on speculative decode stopping steps: Scheduler._update_request_with_output omitted kv_cache_manager.cache_blocks when a running request crossed a block boundary via accepted draft tokens on the same step that stopped the request, and AsyncScheduler._update_request_with_output lacked a staleness and num_tokens clamp guard.

Fix all three gaps:
- In SlidingWindowManager.cache_blocks, retain the active decode frontier (resend_lo, resend_hi, aligned_ext) SWA tail blocks across 256-token MLA boundaries while recycling obsolete intermediate non-segment decode-frontier SWA blocks (un-hashing and prepending to the scratch front of free_block_queue via prepend_n), leaving only the final turn endpoint SWA checkpoint cached at turn completion alongside sparse segment checkpoints.
- Track per-request retained SWA checkpoints (_req_retained_blocks) and prefix-chain inheritance (_block_prefix_chain) in SlidingWindowManager, refresh free retained SWA checkpoints in descending token order on cache hit, sliding-window advance, and request free, and order KVCacheCoordinator.pop_blocks_for_free and free across groups by (-end_token, is_sparse, group_id, -blk_idx) so eviction proceeds strictly from tail to root and full-attention blocks at a given token position evict before sparse SWA segment checkpoints.
- In Scheduler._update_request_with_output and AsyncScheduler._update_request_with_output, call kv_cache_manager.cache_blocks(request, min(request.num_computed_tokens, request.num_tokens)) whenever a non-stale running request advances num_computed_tokens with zero remaining output placeholders before freeing on stop.

Quality:
Bit- and mathematically identical KV attention and compressor contents; strictly preserves decoded frontier and shared prefix checkpoints across turns and under LRU eviction.

Tests:
- pytest tests/v1/core/test_prefix_cache_retention_probe.py tests/v1/core/test_prefix_caching.py tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py tests/v1/core/test_FullAttentionManager.py tests/v1/core/test_scheduler_Scenarios.py tests/v1/core/test_async_scheduler.py (2679 passed across 2 fresh container boots on sp7).

Upstream status: local fix for hybrid MLA + SWA sparse prefix-cache retention and eviction ordering.
